# UI design system

When creating or updating UI, use `design/islands-va-design-system-guide.pdf` (v1.2) together with `design/tokens.json`. Read the relevant section of the guide before inventing layout, colour, type, or a new component.

- Use token classes (`bg-surface-card`, `text-ink`, `type-*`). Never hard-code hex.
- Sentence case. Verb-first buttons ("Request my team"). Voice is you / we / your VA.
- One sunrise primary action per view. Orange is a fill, never text on a light background.
- Alegreya for display, h1, and h2. Figtree for everything else.
- Reuse `components/ui` and `components/layout`. Add a variant only when a second screen needs it.
- Status is an icon, a word, and a colour together. Inputs have a visible label and are at least 44px tall.

These product decisions stay as they are, even where the PDF differs:

- Theme follows the OS. No theme toggle and no theme cookie.
- The logo is the Sand & Sea mark plus the live wordmark in `components/layout/logo.tsx`.
- Do not build the blog, comments, or newsletter. They are outside the MVP.
- Architecture, auth, validation, and rendering follow `CLAUDE.md`. The PDF's Next.js chapter is not the implementation guide.
